{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CftKUv3o2zKu93kXK2vhb","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"**Yes, build it. Three days of work is cheap, and a randomized test settles the question. But judge it on revenue, not on how many people click Pause.**\n\n**Why it's worth it**\n- About 3,900 people cancelled last quarter (2,400 is 61%). If the survey is representative, roughly 1,500 of them were leaving for a temporary reason, and Cancel is the only option they have today.\n- Showing it on the cancel page limits the downside. Only people already leaving see Pause, so you won't tempt happy subscribers to skip weeks.\n\n**What to watch**\n1. **Counterfactual.** Some travellers who cancel probably come back anyway. Before launch, check how many of the \"travelling\" cancellers resubscribed within 90 days. If many did, Pause mostly moves revenue around and the gain is smaller than 38% suggests.\n2. **Success metric.** Compare the two arms on paid orders or revenue per person over about 90 days, counting from when they reached the cancel page. Pause uptake is a vanity number. Also track how many people cancel when their pause ends.\n3. **Stated reasons may not be the real ones.** \"Seasonal break\" can be a polite cover for price or food fatigue. Those people will pause and then cancel anyway, which is another reason to use the revenue metric.\n4. **Guardrails.** Billing that restarts on its own can cause surprise charges, chargebacks and complaints. Send a reminder before deliveries resume, make the restart date obvious, and track refund requests.\n5. **Timing and power.** At about 650 cancellers a month per arm, a few weeks of enrolment plus a 90-day follow-up is enough to see a meaningful difference. Holiday travel is coming, so this season is a good test but may overstate the effect for the rest of the year.\n\n**Decision rule:** If revenue per canceller in the Pause arm beats control by a material margin and complaints stay flat, roll it out to everyone. Then consider offering Pause in account settings too."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":3192,"cache_read_input_tokens":5018,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":3192},"output_tokens":3,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"544d37ca-22e2-4224-854b-dd9487d45eb3","uuid":"cce991ba-ee5c-4ade-849f-8de2bf622168","timestamp":"2026-10-10T09:28:19.538Z","request_id":"req_011CftKUupPqKNeJ5hZxgsfy"}
